From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:16:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] servicemanager: access by binder uid when built without
 SELinux policy

A device build of servicemanager (__ANDROID__) for a host without
Android's SELinux policy cannot run Access as it is: the constructor
CHECK-aborts when selinux_status_open or getcon fail, getPidcon
CHECK-aborts when called inside a transaction, and every lookup is
denied because no service_contexts exists. The non-__ANDROID__ branch
avoids SELinux but returns a default CallingContext, uid 0, which would
let an app add services.

Under ATL_NO_SELINUX, take the non-__ANDROID__ access decisions but keep
the caller's uid and pid from IPCThreadState, with an empty sid; the
uid checks in ServiceManager (addService refuses app uids) still apply.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ATL-specific: no Soong variant builds servicemanager without SELinux]
Patch-Reason: Access is compiled into servicemanager; the launcher, loader or environment cannot reach it: the constructor aborts before any request on a host without selinuxfs or SELinux contexts, getPidcon aborts inside a transaction, and without service_contexts every lookup is denied; faking SELinux in the environment would mean shipping an Android policy and a kernel LSM the host lacks
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 cmds/servicemanager/Access.cpp | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cmds/servicemanager/Access.cpp b/cmds/servicemanager/Access.cpp
index 6e2abf65e2b0c61251e92b77f75e57584ac5912f..336c1a7dbca02601f10fde66708d3fd8371611f6 100644
--- a/cmds/servicemanager/Access.cpp
+++ b/cmds/servicemanager/Access.cpp
@@ -32,7 +32,10 @@ constexpr bool kIsVendor = true;
 constexpr bool kIsVendor = false;
 #endif
 
-#ifdef __ANDROID__
+// ATL_NO_SELINUX: a device build for a host without Android's SELinux policy. Access is then
+// decided as without __ANDROID__, but the caller keeps its binder uid and pid (ServiceManager
+// refuses addService from app uids by uid alone).
+#if defined(__ANDROID__) && !defined(ATL_NO_SELINUX)
 static std::string getPidcon(pid_t pid) {
     CHECK_EQ(nullptr, IPCThreadState::self()->getServingStackPointer())
             << "Did not get context from PID " << pid
@@ -91,7 +94,7 @@ std::string Access::CallingContext::toDebugString() const {
 }
 
 Access::Access() {
-#ifdef __ANDROID__
+#if defined(__ANDROID__) && !defined(ATL_NO_SELINUX)
     union selinux_callback cb;
 
     cb.func_audit = auditCallback;
@@ -120,7 +123,11 @@ Access::CallingContext Access::getCallingContext() {
     return CallingContext {
         .debugPid = callingPid,
         .uid = ipc->getCallingUid(),
+#ifdef ATL_NO_SELINUX
+        .sid = callingSid ? std::string(callingSid) : std::string(),
+#else
         .sid = callingSid ? std::string(callingSid) : getPidcon(callingPid),
+#endif
     };
 #else
     return CallingContext();
@@ -141,7 +148,7 @@ bool Access::canList(const CallingContext& ctx) {
 
 bool Access::actionAllowed(const CallingContext& sctx, const char* tctx, const char* perm,
         const std::string& tname) {
-#ifdef __ANDROID__
+#if defined(__ANDROID__) && !defined(ATL_NO_SELINUX)
     const char* tclass = "service_manager";
 
     AuditCallbackData data = {
@@ -162,7 +169,7 @@ bool Access::actionAllowed(const CallingContext& sctx, const char* tctx, const c
 }
 
 bool Access::actionAllowedFromLookup(const CallingContext& sctx, const std::string& name, const char *perm) {
-#ifdef __ANDROID__
+#if defined(__ANDROID__) && !defined(ATL_NO_SELINUX)
     char *tctx = nullptr;
     if (selabel_lookup(getSehandle(), &tctx, name.c_str(), SELABEL_CTX_ANDROID_SERVICE) != 0) {
         LOG(ERROR) << "SELinux: No match for " << name << " in service_contexts.\n";
